[{"role": "system", "content": "\nYou are a programming expert. \nYou will be provided with a patch used to fix a bug. \n\nYour task is summarize the modifications made in the patch.\nYour summary should consist of two parts, modifications in each file and their relationships.\n"}, {"role": "user", "content": "From 24b2d930a50662c11918fd0c22931f1448488da4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001\nFrom: Geert Uytterhoeven <geert+renesas@glider.be>\nDate: Mon, 7 Nov 2016 20:10:04 +0100\nSubject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: r8a7794: Use SYSC \"always-on\" PM Domain for sound\n\nHook up the Audio-DMAC and sound device nodes to the SYSC \"always-on\" PM\nDomain, for a more consistent device-power-area description in DT.\n\nCfr. commit 0761ff2ad0c581f3 (\"ARM: dts: r8a7794: Add SYSC PM Domains\").\n\nFixes: 320d6c5a08a4abd3 (\"ARM: dts: r8a7794: add sound support\")\nFixes: 298e4ee3d213a076 (\"ARM: dts: r8a7794: add Audio-DMAC support\")\nSigned-off-by: Geert Uytterhoeven <geert+renesas@glider.be>\nSigned-off-by: Simon Horman <horms+renesas@verge.net.au>\n\ndiff --git a/arch/arm/boot/dts/r8a7794.dtsi b/arch/arm/boot/dts/r8a7794.dtsi\nindex 7d9f0601d3ca..364b4aa8d1c1 100644\n--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/r8a7794.dtsi\n+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/r8a7794.dtsi\n@@ -319,7 +319,7 @@ GIC_SPI 331 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH\n \t\t\t\t  \"ch12\";\n \t\tclocks = <&mstp5_clks R8A7794_CLK_AUDIO_DMAC0>;\n \t\tclock-names = \"fck\";\n-\t\tpower-domains = <&cpg_clocks>;\n+\t\tpower-domains = <&sysc R8A7794_PD_ALWAYS_ON>;\n \t\t#dma-cells = <1>;\n \t\tdma-channels = <13>;\n \t};\n@@ -1485,7 +1485,7 @@ rcar_sound: sound@ec500000 {\n \t\t\t      \"mix.0\", \"mix.1\",\n \t\t\t      \"dvc.0\", \"dvc.1\",\n \t\t\t      \"clk_a\", \"clk_b\", \"clk_c\", \"clk_i\";\n-\t\tpower-domains = <&cpg_clocks>;\n+\t\tpower-domains = <&sysc R8A7794_PD_ALWAYS_ON>;\n \n \t\tstatus = \"disabled\";\n \n-- \n2.25.1\n\n\n\n"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "### Modifications in Each File\n\n1. **File: `arch/arm/boot/dts/r8a7794.dtsi`**\n   - **Modification 1**: In the Audio-DMAC node, the `power-domains` property was changed from `<&cpg_clocks>` to `<&sysc R8A7794_PD_ALWAYS_ON>`.\n   - **Modification 2**: In the sound device node, the `power-domains` property was also changed from `<&cpg_clocks>` to `<&sysc R8A7794_PD_ALWAYS_ON>`.\n\n### Relationships Between Modifications\n\nThe modifications in the `r8a7794.dtsi` file are related as they both involve updating the `power-domains` property for two different components (Audio-DMAC and sound device) to utilize the SYSC \"always-on\" power management domain. This change aims to provide a more consistent and accurate representation of the device's power management in the device tree, ensuring that both components are correctly associated with the always-on power domain for improved power management and functionality."}, {"role": "user", "content": "\nBased on your summary and the commit message in the patch, you need to:\n\n1. analyze the root cause of the bug in detail. \n2. output the file name that is most likely to cause the bug. \n\n\n\nProvide a response strictly in the following format:\nRoot cause:<Root cause>\nfile:<file name> \n\n"}, {"role": "user", "content": "\nBased on your summary and the commit message in the patch, you need to:\n\n1. analyze the root cause of the bug in detail. \n2. output the file name that is most likely to cause the bug. \n\n\n\nProvide a response strictly in the following format:\nRoot cause:<Root cause>\nfile:<file name> \n\n"}, {"llm_patch_file_names": ["arch/arm/boot/dts/r8a7794.dtsi"]}, "begin to deal with arch/arm/boot/dts/r8a7794.dtsi in strategy1", {"full_context_length": 13}, {"role": "system", "content": "You are a programming expert."}, {"role": "user", "content": "\n        You will be given the root cause of a bug, the commit message and the corresponding patch.\n        You need to extract all code statements that lead to the bug from the patch, based on the root cause and the commit message.\n\n        Root cause:\n        The bug was caused by the Audio-DMAC and sound device nodes being incorrectly associated with the `<&cpg_clocks>` power domain instead of the SYSC \"always-on\" power domain. This misconfiguration could lead to inconsistent power management behavior, potentially causing issues with device functionality and power state management.\n        \n        Commit message:\n        ARM: dts: r8a7794: Use SYSC \"always-on\" PM Domain for sound\n\nHook up the Audio-DMAC and sound device nodes to the SYSC \"always-on\" PM\nDomain, for a more consistent device-power-area description in DT.\n\nCfr. commit 0761ff2ad0c581f3 (\"ARM: dts: r8a7794: Add SYSC PM Domains\").\n\nFixes: 320d6c5a08a4abd3 (\"ARM: dts: r8a7794: add sound support\")\nFixes: 298e4ee3d213a076 (\"ARM: dts: r8a7794: add Audio-DMAC support\")\nSigned-off-by: Geert Uytterhoeven <geert+renesas@glider.be>\nSigned-off-by: Simon Horman <horms+renesas@verge.net.au>  \n        \n        Patch:\n         \t\tclocks = <&mstp5_clks R8A7794_CLK_AUDIO_DMAC0>;\n \t\tclock-names = \"fck\";\n-\t\tpower-domains = <&cpg_clocks>;\n+\t\tpower-domains = <&sysc R8A7794_PD_ALWAYS_ON>;\n \t\t#dma-cells = <1>;\n \t\tdma-channels = <13>;\n \t\t\t      \"dvc.0\", \"dvc.1\",\n \t\t\t      \"clk_a\", \"clk_b\", \"clk_c\", \"clk_i\";\n-\t\tpower-domains = <&cpg_clocks>;\n+\t\tpower-domains = <&sysc R8A7794_PD_ALWAYS_ON>;\n \n \t\tstatus = \"disabled\";\n\n        \n        Provide a response strictly in the following format:\n        Code statements:\n        <text1>\n        <text2>\n        ...\n        <textN>\n    "}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Code statements:\n-\t\tpower-domains = <&cpg_clocks>;\n+\t\tpower-domains = <&sysc R8A7794_PD_ALWAYS_ON>;\n-\t\tpower-domains = <&cpg_clocks>;\n+\t\tpower-domains = <&sysc R8A7794_PD_ALWAYS_ON>;"}, {"s1_raw_stmts_infos": [{"buggy_stmt": "-\t\tpower-domains = <&cpg_clocks>;", "file_name": "arch/arm/boot/dts/r8a7794.dtsi", "lineno": 1488, "induce_cid": "320d6c5a08a4abd3990ee4744033ade6ed53d5fb"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\t\tpower-domains = <&sysc R8A7794_PD_ALWAYS_ON>;", "file_name": "arch/arm/boot/dts/r8a7794.dtsi", "lineno": 90, "induce_cid": "25611e4ef5bb290805305d499715a840826462f3"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\t\tpower-domains = <&sysc R8A7794_PD_ALWAYS_ON>;", "file_name": "arch/arm/boot/dts/r8a7794.dtsi", "lineno": 103, "induce_cid": "25611e4ef5bb290805305d499715a840826462f3"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\t\tpower-domains = <&sysc R8A7794_PD_ALWAYS_ON>;", "file_name": "arch/arm/boot/dts/r8a7794.dtsi", "lineno": 116, "induce_cid": "25611e4ef5bb290805305d499715a840826462f3"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\t\tpower-domains = <&sysc R8A7794_PD_ALWAYS_ON>;", "file_name": "arch/arm/boot/dts/r8a7794.dtsi", "lineno": 129, "induce_cid": "25611e4ef5bb290805305d499715a840826462f3"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\t\tpower-domains = <&sysc R8A7794_PD_ALWAYS_ON>;", "file_name": "arch/arm/boot/dts/r8a7794.dtsi", "lineno": 142, "induce_cid": "25611e4ef5bb290805305d499715a840826462f3"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\t\tpower-domains = <&sysc R8A7794_PD_ALWAYS_ON>;", "file_name": "arch/arm/boot/dts/r8a7794.dtsi", "lineno": 155, "induce_cid": "25611e4ef5bb290805305d499715a840826462f3"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\t\tpower-domains = <&sysc R8A7794_PD_ALWAYS_ON>;", "file_name": "arch/arm/boot/dts/r8a7794.dtsi", "lineno": 168, "induce_cid": "25611e4ef5bb290805305d499715a840826462f3"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\t\tpower-domains = <&sysc R8A7794_PD_ALWAYS_ON>;", "file_name": "arch/arm/boot/dts/r8a7794.dtsi", "lineno": 178, "induce_cid": "25611e4ef5bb290805305d499715a840826462f3"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\t\tpower-domains = <&sysc R8A7794_PD_ALWAYS_ON>;", "file_name": "arch/arm/boot/dts/r8a7794.dtsi", "lineno": 198, "induce_cid": "25611e4ef5bb290805305d499715a840826462f3"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\t\tpower-domains = <&sysc R8A7794_PD_ALWAYS_ON>;", "file_name": "arch/arm/boot/dts/r8a7794.dtsi", "lineno": 229, "induce_cid": "25611e4ef5bb290805305d499715a840826462f3"}, {"buggy_stmt": "+\t\tpower-domains = <&sysc R8A7794_PD_ALWAYS_ON>;", "file_name": "arch/a